    <h1>Hosted terms — unapproved draft</h1>
    <p class="lede"><strong>Not in force.</strong> Montral Cloud is not publicly launched or accepting customers. The text below is an unapproved working draft for a possible future hosted service, not a contract or a statement that any hosted service operates. It does not apply to the open-source Community code or to deployments run by other operators. Legal review and owner authorization are required before any hosted service can publish binding terms.</p>

    <h2>The service and the source code</h2>
    <p>Montral's source code is released under the MIT License and can be self-hosted under that license. The remaining clauses on this page are illustrative drafts only and are not an effective agreement for any service. An operator of a separate self-hosted deployment must provide its own legal information as appropriate.</p>

    <h2>Your account</h2>
    <p>You are responsible for your account, for keeping your password and API keys secret, and for everything done through them. Provide accurate information and tell us promptly if you suspect unauthorised access. You must be at least 16 years old.</p>

    <h2>Acceptable use</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Only probe what you are authorised to probe.</strong> Monitors must target systems you own or have explicit permission to test.</li>
      <li>Do not use monitors, heartbeat endpoints or alert channels to attack, scan, overload or harass third parties, or to run denial-of-service traffic, including by setting very short intervals against systems that are not yours.</li>
      <li>Do not use the service to send spam or unsolicited messages through alert channels or status page subscriptions, or to host unlawful, infringing or deceptive content on status pages.</li>
      <li>Do not try to break, probe or circumvent the service's security, rate limits or other users' data, and do not overload the API.</li>
      <li>Do not use the service to reach private or internal addresses you are not permitted to access.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>You are responsible for the content of your status pages and the messages you send to subscribers.</p>

    <h2>Availability and no warranty</h2>
    <p>We run the service on a best-effort basis. It is provided "as is" and "as available", without warranties of any kind, express or implied, including merchantability, fitness for a particular purpose and non-infringement. We do not guarantee uninterrupted or error-free operation, that checks will run on time, or that alerts will be delivered. Do not rely on Montral as the only means of detecting failures in safety-critical systems.</p>

    <h2>Suspension and termination</h2>
    <p>You can stop using the service and delete your account at any time. We may suspend or terminate accounts that violate these terms, put the service or others at risk, or are abandoned, and where practical we will tell you why. After termination your data is deleted as described in the <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>.</p>

    <h2>Limitation of liability</h2>
    <p>To the extent permitted by law, the Montral contributors are not liable for indirect, incidental, special, consequential or punitive damages, or for lost profits, revenue, data or business, arising from your use of the service, including missed or delayed alerts and outages that go undetected. Our total liability for any claim is limited to the greater of the amount you paid us in the previous twelve months and USD 50. Nothing here excludes liability that cannot be excluded by law.</p>

    <h2>Your content</h2>
    <p>You keep ownership of the data and content you put into the service. You grant us the limited right to store, process and display it as needed to operate the service for you, including publishing your status pages as you configure them.</p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>We may update these terms and the service. If a change is material we will update the date below and, where practical, notify you by email. Continuing to use the service after a change means you accept the new terms.</p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>Montral contributors &middot; A verified legal contact will be published before any hosted launch.</p>
